# Public build-time SEO configuration. Rebuild after changes.
# Set to the actual production origin (https:// followed by your domain).
# Leave blank until the production domain is confirmed. No domain is invented.
VITE_SITE_URL=

# Keep false on development and preview deployments. Enable only after approving
# public content. Demo catalogue/detail pages remain noindex independently.
VITE_SEO_INDEXABLE=false

# Vercel setup:
# - Runtime: Node.js 24.x; framework preset: Other (configured in vercel.json).
# - Install/build commands are supplied by vercel.json using pinned pnpm via Corepack.
# - Leave Output Directory unset: Nitro emits the .vercel/output Build Output API.
# - Add VITE_SITE_URL and VITE_SEO_INDEXABLE in Vercel Project Settings.
# - VITE_SITE_URL is the confirmed production origin, not a random preview URL.
# - Preview deployments are forced to noindex even if the production flag is true.
# - Environment changes require a new deployment/build.
# - pnpm build:vercel validates the Vercel output locally; it does not deploy.
# - pnpm build && pnpm start continues to run the standalone Node server locally.
